From 4398e32e4251b4975166d2a49736475675cb5660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:51:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Play an audio preview when the YouTube player can't run
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

iTunes previews now work in in-app browsers, but YouTube tracks stayed
silent. Two causes: the player was built only after the tap (script fetch,
then onReady), so playVideo() landed well outside the activation window; and
priming an <audio> element grants nothing to a cross-origin iframe.

- warmYouTube() builds the player ahead of the tap, and a warm player loads
  and starts the video synchronously, inside the gesture.
- In an in-app browser the embedded player is skipped entirely — it stalls
  and then fails — and a 30-second preview of the same track plays instead.
- Anywhere else, a player that fails to start (embed disabled, blocked,
  offline) falls back the same way rather than sitting silent.

Verified with an Instagram user agent: no request to youtube.com is made,
the toast explains the swap, and audio plays. The control run attempts
YouTube first and falls back when it can't load. Real YouTube playback is
unreachable from this sandbox, so that success path is unverified here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018JjAD7WNZmP26cnkvFDZws
